This experiment is about connecting a Python program to a Large Language Model using the Gemini API. Instead of manually asking questions in a chatbot, we write Python code that sends a prompt to the AI model and receives its response automatically.
Installed the google-genai and python-dotenv packages.
Created a .env file to store the Gemini API key.
Used load_dotenv() to load the API key into the program.
Created a Gemini client using the API key.
Sent a prompt asking the model to explain Generative AI with five real-world examples.
Printed the generated response in the terminal.
